// HW3 — Collaborative Filtering
//
// Missing-value strategy (week3/readme.md section 6), chosen EXACTLY ONE and
// applied consistently in every similarity below:
//
//   CO-RATED ENTRIES ONLY — cosine similarity looks at indices where BOTH
//   vectors have a non-zero rating; missing entries are skipped, never
//   filled. Chosen because it is the simplest strategy that invents no
//   evidence: the matrix is 93.7% sparse and mostly missing-not-at-random,
//   and imputing means would manufacture agreement out of absence. The
//   alternatives (mean imputation, co-rated-count weighting) and matrix
//   factorization are still measured against this choice in
//   week3/analysis.mjs and discussed in week3/prompt.md.
//
// MIN_SUPPORT below is a CANDIDATE FILTER, not a second missing-value
// strategy: a candidate is only recommended/predicted if its estimate rests
// on at least MIN_SUPPORT contributing ratings (user-based: neighbours who
// rated the movie; item-based: of the user's rated movies with positive
// similarity). Without it, an obscure movie rated 5 by its single co-rater
// with the active user gets a perfect 5.0 prediction and dominates Top-5.
